    "created_at": "2019-09-09T13:15:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-09T13:15:10Z",
    "body": "It is not clear to me what this bug covers at this point.\r\n\r\n- The `onanimation*` and `ontransition*` event handlers are nowadays spec'd in [css-animations-1](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-animations-1/#event-handlers-on-elements-document-objects-and-window-objects) and [css-transitions-1](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-transitions-1/#event-handlers-on-elements-document-objects-and-window-objects)\r\n- Mention was made of `document.createEvent(\"WebKitTransitionEvent\")`: Chromium dropped both WebKitTransitionEvent and WebKitAnimationEvent in the last few years: [1](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!searchin/blink-dev/WebkitTransitionEvent|sort:date/blink-dev/mMJ5vh7AVyk/rw2c2NY_BQAJ), [2](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!searchin/blink-dev/WebkitTransitionEvent|sort:date/blink-dev/0Szv8vDQh_c/2bI2es2nBwAJ), [3](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!searchin/blink-dev/WebKitAnimationEvent|sort:date/blink-dev/VlbJIDOIIqw/ynyPNto_BQAJ), [4](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/forum/#!searchin/blink-dev/WebKitAnimationEvent|sort:date/blink-dev/EgMUDqySZwE/idvX9_ZCCQAJ)\r\n\r\nIt seems this should be closed in favour of #118 , but does anyone know a reason to keep this open and separate?",
